  "SelectedConfigIndex": 1,
  "Note": "# Options for the Lategame Sample Config\n<span data-color=\"red\">**Use this sellfile at your own risk.**</span>  <span data-color=\"orange\">Every account is different.</span>   \n<span data-color=\"green\">It's recommended to drive this sellfile together with the real **RSL Helper** database. This helps retaining **unique** gear pieces (gear pieces you do not have many of). The **Help** explains how to easily get the database into **RSL Helper Sellfile Creator**.</span>   \n\nIn this sellfile we want to offer some options to allow you to configure it a little bit for your own needs.   \n## \nWith these options you can set defaults according to your account progression. You can set more detailed option further below or even modify all rules outside of this dialog.\n<!-- config-options [wholeline columns=4]\n  q \"Which account level do you think you have?\"\n  cb \"`Lategame`\" \"I can finish all **Normal** game modes and a lot of the stages in any **Hard** mode.\nDifferent than accessories, **5★** and **6★ Rare** gear is usually sold!\"\n * id=lategame ^lategame  +marius_open +fwh_no +la_no +eg_no +o5s_late4 +o6s_late4 +o6c_yes16 !o5_lvlcap !o6_lvlcap {}\n  cb \"`Endgame`\" \"I can finish all **Hard** game modes including **Cursed City** / **Soulcross** and **Faction Wars,** and **all my used champs are already equipped properly.**\nDifferent than accessories, **5★** and **6★ Rare** gear is usually sold!\" id=endgame ^endgame +marius_finished +fwh_yes16 +la_yes16 +eg_yes16 +o5s_early +o6s_early +o6c_yes16 +o5_lvlcap +o6_lvlcap {}\n  cb \"`Endgame+`\" \"I can finish everything easily and want to only keep the best of the best gear.\nDifferent than accessories, **5★** and **6★ Rare** gear is usually sold!\" id=kraken ^kraken +marius_finished +fwh_yes +la_yes +eg_yes +o5s_early +o6s_early +o6c_yes16 +o5_lvlcap +o6_lvlcap {}\n-->\n##\nThese rules decide whether a piece is **protected** at its current level. Currently in `RSL Helper` `Auto-sell` only applies to fresh drops if that feature is enabled there. \n<!-- config-options\n  q \"Are you done with all progressive missions for Marius?\"\nRegardless of your answer, exceptionally good pieces are always protected.\"\n  rb \"`No`\" \"Protect all Impulse and Zeal drops\" * id=marius_open { @tag=marius { export=active } }\n  rb \"`Yes`\" \"Allow auto-sell for weak Impulse and Zeal drops (unless protected elsewhere)\" id=marius_finished { export=disabled }\n-->\n<!-- config-options\n  q \"Did you finish Faction Wars in Hard mode?\n  This question targets utility gear sets like **Stun**, **Provoke**, **Toxic**, etc...\nRegardless of your answer, exceptionally good pieces are always protected.\"\n  rb \"`No`\" \"Protect utility drops at any level (0-16)\" * id=fwh_no { @tag=fwhard { export=active lvl=0-16 } }\n  rb \"`Yes`\" \"Protect only level 16 utility pieces\" id=fwh_yes16 { @tag=fwhard { export=active lvl=16 } }\n  rb \"`Yes!`\" \"Treat this gear like normal drops (no extra protection)\" id=fwh_yes { @tag=fwhard { export=disabled } }\n-->\n<!-- config-options\n  q \"Do you play and win Live Arena and Siege a lot?\n  This question targets mediocre **Feral**, **Stonecleaver**, **Rebirth** gear.\nRegardless of your answer, exceptionally good pieces are always protected.\"\n  rb \"`No`\" \"Protect Live Arena and Siege drops\" * id=la_no { @tag=pvpgear { export=active lvl=0-16 } }\n  rb \"`Yes`\" \"But still protect existing level 16 mediocre pieces\" id=la_yes16 { @tag=pvpgear { export=active lvl=16 } }\n  rb \"`Yes!`\" \"Treat this gear like normal limited-set drops (no extra protection)\" id=la_yes { @tag=pvpgear { export=disabled } }\n-->\n<!-- config-options\n  q \"Do you safely farm all dungeon hard stages 10 **and** finish all 101 stages of Cursed City (hard) always completely **and** have enough great gear to equip your useful champs completely?\n  This question targets all gear sets except utility and Live Arena sets.\nRegardless of your answer, exceptionally good pieces are always protected.\"\n  rb \"`No`\" \"Protect less-optimal drops\" * id=eg_no { @tag=mediocre { export=active lvl=0-16 } }\n  rb  \"`Yes`\" \"But still protect existing level 16 mediocre pieces\" id=eg_yes16 { @tag=mediocre { export=active lvl=16 } }\n  rb \"`Yes!`\" \"Allow auto-sell for mediocre drops (unless protected elsewhere)\" id=eg_yes { @tag=mediocre { export=disabled } }\n-->\n##\nSometimes a gear piece is practically useless because of bad stats, yet the gear set is useful and we might want to consider using  `Chaos Ore` to `rework` it later with a chance to get 3× or 4× in the `Speed` substat.\n<!-- config-options\n  q \"Do you want to keep low‑quality `5★` pieces to roll them up for a `Chaos Ore` `rework` later?\nThis question targets scarce gear sets like **Merciless**, **Stoneskin**, **Mercurial** (etc) and gear-sets providing Speed as gear set bonus.\"\n  rb \"Protect gear that can still reach **3×** rolls by **level 12** (**≥ Epic**)\" * id=o5s_early { @tag=ore3x5e { export=active keep=early } }\n  rb \"Protect gear that can still reach **4×** rolls by **level 16** (**≥ Legendary**)\" id=o5s_late4 { @tag=ore3x5e { export=disabled } }\n  rb \"Sell bad **5★** gear even if it has a chance or even rolled 3× or 4× on a single substat\" id=o5s_no { @tag=ore3x5e { export=disabled } @tag=ore3x5l { export=disabled } }\n  cb \"Cap level range to 12-16, so only gear which naturally rolled **3×**/**4×** will be protected from auto-sell\" id=o5_lvlcap { @tag=ore3x5e { lvl=12-16 } }\n-->\n<!-- config-options\n  q \"Do you want to keep low‑quality `6★`pieces to roll them up for a `Chaos Ore` `rework` later?\nThis question targets scarce gear sets like **Merciless**, **Stoneskin**, **Mercurial** (etc) and gear-sets providing Speed as gear set bonus.\"\n  rb \"Protect gear that can still reach **3×** rolls by **level 12** (**≥ Epic**)\" * id=o6s_early { @tag=ore3x6e { export=active keep=early } }\n  rb \"Protect gear that can still reach **4×** rolls by **level 16** (**≥ Legendary**)\" id=o6s_late4 { @tag=ore3x6e { export=disabled } }\n  rb \"Sell bad **6★** gear even if it has a chance or even rolled 3× or 4× on a single substat\"  id=o6s_no { @tag=ore3x6e { export=disabled } @tag=ore3x6l { export=disabled } }\n  cb \"Cap level range to 12-16, so only gear which naturally rolled **3×**/**4×** will be protected from auto-sell\" id=o6_lvlcap { @tag=ore3x6e  { lvl=12-16 } }\n-->\n<!-- config-options\n  q \"Do you want to keep low‑quality **6★** pieces to roll them up for a `Chaos Ore` `rework` later?\nThis question targets any usually useful set other than those listed in the 2 other options.\"\n  rb \"Protect gear which can roll **4×** in a single substat (**≥ Legendary**)\" id=o6c_yes { @tag=ore4x6 { export=active lvl=0-16 substatmin=4 } }\n  rb \"Protect gear which can roll **5×** in a single substat (**Mythical** only)\" id=o6c_yesMyth { @tag=ore4x6 { export=active lvl=0-16 substatmin=5 } }\n  rb \"Protect gear which is currently **level 16** and has **≥ 4×** rolls in a single substat\" * id=o6c_yes16 { @tag=ore4x6e { export=active lvl=16 substatmin=4 } }\n  rb \"Sell bad **6★** gear even if it has a chance or even rolled 4× or 5× on a single substat\" id=o6c_no { @tag=ore4x6 { export=disabled substatmin=4 } }\n-->\n\n---\n# Notes for the Lategame Sample Config\nThis note documents the sample configuration bundled with `RSL Helper Sellfile Creator`. It reflects late endgame priorities as of 08 February 2026 and focuses on protecting high-impact pieces while safely auto-selling filler.\n\nThe file relies on a whitelist strategy. Every rule marked `keep` protects something specific; anything not protected is eligible for auto-sell. \n<span data-color=\"orange\">The baseline assumes all `5★ Rare` gear (and worse) is disposable, so we almost never protect any `5★` gear.</span>\n\n<span data-color=\"green\">Feel free to duplicate configs, tweak filters, and use the multi-select bulk editor to adapt the file to a midgame account.</span>  \n\n---\n## Metasets\nMetasets provide named collections of gear sets so multiple configs can reference the same intent. When Raid adds a new set, decide which metasets it belongs to based on the set bonus or special effect, update the metaset once, and re-export the `Sellfile`. The referencing configs pick up the change automatically. Some sets appear in more than one metaset by design.\n\n- **Nuker - Limited Sets** - Cruel, Lethal, Instinct, Zeal, Merciless, Slayer, Stonecleaver.\n- **Nuker** - Crit Damage, Savage, Cruel, Lethal, Stoneskin, Killstroke, Instinct, Zeal, Merciless, Slayer, Stonecleaver, Mercurial.\n- **Support - Limited Sets** - Bolster, Impulse, Supersonic, Merciless, Feral, Pinpoint, Rebirth, Chronophage.\n- **Need 4 Speed** - Speed, Divine Speed, Swift Parry, Perception, Protection, Stoneskin, Impulse, Righteous, Supersonic, Merciless, Feral, Pinpoint, Rebirth, Chronophage, Mercurial.\n- **Debuffer** - Speed, Accuracy, Divine Speed, Perception, Protection, Stoneskin, Impulse, Righteous, Supersonic, Feral, Pinpoint, Rebirth, Chronophage, Mercurial.\n- **Survivability** - Regeneration, Immunity, Shield, Immortal, Divine Speed, Swift Parry, Deflection, Resilience, Untouchable, Frostbite, Guardian, Fortitude, Protection, Stoneskin, Bolster, Defiant, Righteous, Supersonic, Feral, Pinpoint, Rebirth, Chronophage, Mercurial.\n- **Extra Turn** - Relentless, Reflex, Merciless.\n- **Utility** - Lifesteal, Daze, Cursed, Frost, Destroy, Stun, Toxic, Provoke, Retaliation, Affinitybreaker, Frostbite, Bloodthirst.\n- **Accessory Specific** - Protection, Stoneskin, Supersonic, Merciless, Slayer, Feral, Pinpoint, Stonecleaver, Rebirth, Chronophage, Mercurial, Refresh, Cleansing, Bloodshield, Reaction, Revenge.\n- **Accessory Specific - Modern** - Protection, Stoneskin, Supersonic, Merciless, Slayer, Feral, Pinpoint, Stonecleaver, Rebirth, Chronophage, Mercurial.\n- **Debuffer - Limited Sets** - Stoneskin, Impulse, Righteous, Supersonic, Merciless, Feral, Pinpoint, Chronophage, Mercurial, Refresh, Reaction.\n- **Useless** - Life, Offense, Defense, Divine Offense.\n\n---\n## Config structure\n`RSL Helper Sellfile Creator` calls each rule blueprint a `Config`. A `Config` defines filters for set, slot, rank, rarity, level, stats, faction, and roll quality, plus the desired outcome (`keep` for protection or `sell` to allow auto-sell). When you export, the builder converts every config into one or more HSF rule rows. These are the same rows you can inspect in `Sellfile Preview` or inside `RSL Helper`.\n\n### General\nGeneral configs cover account-wide needs: like for the `Marius` objectives (enabled depending on the config options shown further above), safeguards for existing `4×` rolls, and `Chaos Ore` candidates. For the rarest sets we chase at least a `3×` roll on a relevant substat for `5★` and `6★` items so we can `rework` them with `Chaos Ore` into something useful.  \n<span data-color=\"red\">Flat `HP/ATK/DEF` substats cannot be evaluated via raw values, so the roll-count checkpoints are customized by averages.</span>\n\nThis group of configs looks like this:\n<!-- recipes-re: \"^Optional: Marius Sets$\" -->\n<!-- recipes-re: \"^\\[.*\\] Chaos Ore$\" -->\n\n### Low-value gear\nFirst, we clear space by targeting weak sets. Anything already leveled to 16 can stay if it meets the existing-roll thresholds, but fresh drops from those sets (`level 0-8`) are auto-sold depending on the config options set above.  \nUnless `Keep Unique`-rules apply, we also auto-sell newly acquired `5★ Rare` gear on sight, because investing silver there rarely pays off in late lategame accounts.  `Keep Unique`-rules are explained further below.\n<!-- recipes-re: \"^Low (Value|Value Sets|Rank/Rarity)$\" -->\n\n### Speed focused\nThe most important substat is `SPD`.  \nFollowing configs look for strong `SPD` substat rolls regardless of the set. The focus here is substat speed, not the main stat.  \n<!-- recipes-re: \"^Speed - Primary$|^Speed - Limited Sets$\" -->\n\n### Damage / Survivability / Debuffer focus\nThe remaining configs are grouped by stat pattern so we can balance silver spend against set scarcity:\n\n- `Damage` chases aggressive mixes of `SPD`/`CR%`/`CDMG%`.\n- `Survivability` looks for `SPD`/`HP%`/`DEF%`/`RES` blends.\n- `Debuffer` targets `SPD`/`ACC` combinations.\n\nWe are not looking for only these substat patterns though, but they are the core substats for that particular role.\n\n#### Primary Rolls\nThese configs are set-agnostic and expect strong early rolls. If a piece starts hot, it stays, even in not-so-great gear-sets.\n<!-- recipes-re: \"^(Damage|Survivability|Debuffer) - Primary.*$\" -->\n\n#### Limited Sets\nUltra-rare sets deserve extra leeway. These configs protect middling substats when the gear-set supply itself is the bottleneck. Bomb champions receive additional coverage inside this group as well.\n<!-- recipes-re: \"^(Damage|Survivability|Debuffer) - Limited Sets$|^Debuffer - Bomber Focus$\" -->\n\n#### Secondary Rolls\nIf an item misses the ideal early rolls, these configs give it a second chance when it belongs to a supportive gear-set. They always specify a metaset and only tolerate pieces whose gear-set bonus aligns with the stat goals. Bomb-focused builds get their own hooks here.\n<!-- recipes-re: \"^(Damage|Survivability|Debuffer) - Secondary.*$\" -->\n\n### Utility gear\nNiche sets (`Stun`, `Provoke`, `Toxic`, etc.) rarely see play, but they can solve specific PvE problems. These configs **protect anything at `level 16`** without flat substats so long as it belongs to the `Utility` metaset. \nIf you did not finished `Faction Wars Hard` yet, the above config option will essentially **extend the level range to `0-16`** .  \nThe general-purpose configs above will still protect any standout rolls.  \n<!-- recipes-re: \"^Utility$\" -->\n\n### Super-rare gear\nLive Arena, Siege, and other time-gated modes drip-feed some sets. To avoid regretting a sale months later, this block protects `Feral`, `Stonecleaver`, `Rebirth`, and similar drops even if the substats need work.\n<!-- recipes-re: \"^Scarce Sets.*$\" -->\n\n### Accessories\nAccessories follow three simple rules:\n\n- Banners should show `SPD` as substat.\n- Amulets chase `RES`/`ACC` rolls or a single flat substat when the main stat already covers the rest.\n- Rings need substats that reinforce the main stat.\n\nAgain, we are not looking for only these substat patterns though, but they are the core substats for that particular slot.\n\n<!-- recipes-re: \"^(Banner|Amulet|Ring) - (Primary( \\((UDK)\\))?)$\" -->\n\nLimited-set accessories get slightly relaxed thresholds because replacing them is harder. Expect wider disagreements here as every accounts progression is different, so tailor these configs to your champions.\n<!-- recipes-re: \"^(Banner|Amulet|Ring) - Limited Sets$\" -->\n\n---\n## Final Sell\n`Final Sell` generates `sell` rows (auto-sell rules) for artifacts and accessories for all levels. Anything that fails every earlier `keep` rule is flagged before more silver is wasted.  \n\n---\n## Keep Unique Rules\n`Keep Unique` protects at least one piece per combination even when your normal `Keep` configs wouldn’t. It’s like a \"Bad Luck\" protection.  \n\nNote: Keep Unique only works when you’ve loaded the `RSL Helper` database, and they never pick a favorite unless you set one or more substats - if multiple items satisfy the same combination, all of them are kept.  \n\nWe want to ensure that we keep banners which have `SPD` on them. We keep at least 3 of each gear-set.  \nWe also want to keep at least one `ATK` amulet with `ACC` on it.  \nThere are several more of these type of rules here which ensure we have a baseline of artifacts and accessories to choose from.\n<!-- keep-uniques-re:\"Reserve\" -->\n\nThe other keep unique rules are to protect at least 1 `ATK`, `HP`, `DEF` ring and likewise 1 of each amulet main-stat, and 1 of each banner main-stat, for each 9-piece set (and the old 1 piece gear-sets) of each faction.  \nFurthermore we protect at least 5 rings/amulets/banners for each 9-piece set of each faction so that we can equip a full faction wars team.\n<!-- keep-uniques-re:\"Unique.*Accessories\" -->\n\nThe next keep-uniques rules are similar to above but for Artifacts instead of Accessoires, and we limited it to sets which are not terrible.  \n<!-- keep-uniques-re: \"Unique.*Artifacts\"-->\n\nThe last keep-unique rules accompany the configs for utilities. We protect 2 of each good mainstat per slot of utility-sets to ensure we have gear for any special upcoming events or game updates.   \n<!-- keep-uniques-re: \"Unique.*Utilities\" -->\n---\nThanks for using `RSL Helper Sellfile Creator`.  \n**Good luck with your farming. May the 4× SPD rolls bless your account!**"
}
